{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/trpc/trpc/pulls/4948","id":1567776100,"node_id":"PR_kwDOELj1_s5dcl1k","html_url":"https://github.com/trpc/trpc/pull/4948","diff_url":"https://github.com/trpc/trpc/pull/4948.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/trpc/trpc/pull/4948.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/trpc/trpc/issues/4948","number":4948,"state":"closed","locked":true,"title":"fix(server): merge _input_out when using standalone middlewares","user":{"login":"jussisaurio","id":22619982,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIyNjE5OTgy","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/22619982?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jussisaurio","html_url":"https://github.com/jussisaurio","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jussisaurio/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jussisaurio/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jussisaurio/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jussisaurio/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jussisaurio/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jussisaurio/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jussisaurio/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jussisaurio/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jussisaurio/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"Closes #4947\r\n\r\n## 🎯 Changes\r\n\r\nThere was a problem in the current implementation of `experimental_standaloneMiddleware`\r\nwhere the `input` type was not merged properly in the middleware chain.\r\n\r\nExample:\r\n\r\n```\r\n  const t = initTRPC.create();\r\n  const schemaA = z.object({ valueA: z.string() });\r\n  const schemaB = z.object({ valueB: z.string() });\r\n\r\n  const mw1 = experimental_standaloneMiddleware<{\r\n    input: z.infer<typeof schemaA>;\r\n  }>().create((opts) => {\r\n    return opts.next();\r\n  });\r\n\r\n  const mw2 = experimental_standaloneMiddleware<{\r\n    input: z.infer<typeof schemaB>;\r\n  }>().create((opts) => {\r\n    return opts.next();\r\n  });\r\n\r\n  const combinedInputThatSatisfiesBothMiddlewares = z.object({\r\n    valueA: z.string(),\r\n    valueB: z.string(),\r\n  })\r\n\r\n  t.procedure\r\n    .input(combinedInputThatSatisfiesBothMiddlewares)\r\n    .use(mw1)\r\n    .use(mw2) // <-- error: input only has { valueA: string }\r\n    .query(\r\n      ({\r\n        input: { valueA, valueB }, // <-- error: input only has { valueB: string }\r\n      }) =>\r\n        `valueA: ${valueA}, valueB: ${valueB}`,\r\n    );\r\n```\r\n\r\nFunnily enough, since tRPC merges multiple .input() schemas under the hood, it was\r\npossible to never encounter this problem if you e.g. defined another .input() parser\r\nafter a standalone middleware, e.g.:\r\n\r\n```\r\nt.input(onlyA).use(requiresAMiddleware).input(otherStuff).query(opts => /* opts.input has merged onlyA and otherStuff! */\r\n```\r\n\r\nThis commits fixes the problem by merging `_input_out` whenever necessary.\r\n\r\n## ✅ Checklist\r\n\r\n- [x] I have followed the steps listed in the [Contributing guide](https://github.com/trpc/trpc/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md).\r\n- [x] If necessary, I have added documentation related to the changes made.\r\n- [x] I have added or updated the tests related to the changes made.\r\n","created_at":"2023-10-21T14:45:37Z","updated_at":"2023-11-23T18:02:11Z","closed_at":"2023-10-24T15:48:14Z","merged_at":"2023-10-24T15:48:14Z","merge_commit_sha":"2f55f7eb788658140a163496b437412ceeb3be8e","assignees":[],"requested_reviewers":[],"requested_teams":[],"labels":[{"id":2728304521,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwyNzI4MzA0NTIx","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/trpc/trpc/labels/@trpc/server","name":"@trpc/server","color":"9BE78E","default":false,"description":"","archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":4328853984,"node_id":"LA_kwDOELj1_s8AAAABAgUR4A","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/trpc/trpc/labels/%F0%9F%95%B8%20www","name":"🕸 www","color":"666FF9","default":false,"description":"Stuff to do with the website (`/www` folder)","archived_at":null,"archived_by":null}],"milestone":null,"draft":false,"commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/trpc/trpc/pulls/4948/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/trpc/trpc/pulls/4948/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/trpc/trpc/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/trpc/trpc/issues/4948/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/trpc/trpc/statuses/39c272386e9f561ceccb3c3f0c62ed34f828bea7","head":{"label":"jussisaurio:fix-4947-standalone-mw-merge-inputs","ref":"fix-4947-standalone-mw-merge-inputs","sha":"39c272386e9f561ceccb3c3f0c62ed34f828bea7","user":{"login":"jussisaurio","id":22619982,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIyNjE5OTgy","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/22619982?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jussisaurio","html_url":"https://github.com/jussisaurio","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jussisaurio/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jussisaurio/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jussisaurio/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jussisaurio/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jussisaurio/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jussisaurio/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jussisaurio/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jussisaurio/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jussisaurio/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"repo":{"id":677694624,"node_id":"R_kgDOKGTMoA","name":"trpc","full_name":"jussisaurio/trpc","private":false,"owner":{"login":"jussisaurio","id":22619982,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIyNjE5OTgy","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2